{"name":"Havana","hex":"#3b2b2c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Havana","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The capital city of Cuba.\n\n The Cuban government.","The Cuban government."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of large cigar produced in Cuba."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Havana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Havana","blocks":[{"text":"Havana is the capital and largest city of Cuba. The heart of La Habana Province, Havana is the country's main port and commercial center. It is the most populous city, the largest by area, and the second-largest metropolitan area in the Caribbean region. The population in 2021 was 2,142,939 inhabitants, and its area is 728.26 km2 (281.18 sq mi) for the capital city and 8,475.57 km2 for the metropolitan zone. Its official population however had dropped to 1,749,964 inhabitants by the end of 2024."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/DJI_0197_crp_wiki.jpg/330px-DJI_0197_crp_wiki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Havana","wikidata":"Q1563"},{"title":"Havana (Camila Cabello song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Havana\" is a song by American singer Camila Cabello featuring American rapper Young Thug, from her debut studio album Camila (2018). It was released on August 3, 2017, alongside \"OMG\" initially as a promotional single; it was later serviced to radio on September 8, 2017, as a single. Due to its rising success, \"Havana\" later became the official lead single of Camila, replacing \"Crying in the Club\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/98/Havana_%28featuring_Young_Thug%29_%28Official_Single_Cover%29_by_Camila_Cabello.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Havana_(Camila_Cabello_song)","wikidata":"Q35282195"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip